<title>FRANCE: Juppe says mark-franc parity should not be changed.</title>
<headline>Juppe says mark-franc parity should not be changed.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Prime Minister Alain Juppe said on Wednesday he did not believe the exchange rate between the German mark and the French franc should be changed.</p>
<p>Speaking in a parliamentary debate on European Union, Juppe said &quot;Should the franc-mark parity be changed? I don't think so. Any devaluation is an national impoverishment.&quot;</p>
</text>
